  concept: "Authored objective: Stay stopped after the jam clears.\nAuthored requirement:
    Recorded from the solved timer voltage and motor state during the jam test. voltage
    \u2265 4.8 V. voltage \u2264 5.2 V.\nGeneral teaching principle: Motor behavior
    depends on drive conditions, load, feedback and protective limits; test the observed
    state at each authored checkpoint.\nOnly fresh, authoritative game evidence can
    establish that this objective is complete."
  analogy: A controlled wheel under varying load shows why a command does not always
    equal actual speed.
